<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, here is what we have been working on, for Raders background and Possible Vics. I know it&#39;s long sorry , but can you help us fill in any of the blanks Thanks Sheila <BR>2005&#42;  <BR>1/27: WPD recovers BTK&#39;s Post Toasties cereal box communique as a result of letter sent to KAKE tv; the letter indicates yet another communique that WPD has overlooked and quickly locates; both drops are left in rural areas far afield of BTK&#39;s previously understood boundaries; contents not revealed <BR>|- 1/31: Melissa Scott &#40;Valley Center, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified &#40;autopsy results not complete/released; police tight lipped&#41;, children unharmed [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1107462969820" target=_top>http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1107462 969820</a>&#62; <BR>|- 2/3: KAKE tv receives postcard from BTK, it expresses condolensces for the colds 2 news casters suffer, though the rest of the content is not revealed <BR>|- 2/3: KSAS tv receives manilla envelope with undisclosed message and objects. KSAS is a FOX affiliate. [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm</a>&#62; <BR>|- 2/25 - 2/26: WPD arrests Dennis Rader off tip from daughter Kerri, hold press conference declaring they have a DNA match for Rader as BTK <BR>2004&#42;  <BR>3/19: BTK letter received by The Wichita Eagle containing photocopy of photos of the Wegerle crime scene and of Vicki&#39;s driver&#39;s license <BR>|- 4/7: KSN tv receives anonymous letter containing unidentified baby photo &#40;view at catchbtk.com &#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/16.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/16.html</a>&#62;&#41;; presumed to be from BTK <BR>|- 5/5: KAKE tv receives &#34;The BTK Story&#34;, a rambling autobiography patterned after Crime Library&#39;s BTK feature &#60;<a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/index_1.html" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/index_1.html</a>&#62;, included are two phoney photo ID&#39;s <BR>|- 6/17: WPD receives letter from BTK concerning Otero murders; a second letter is discovered the same day at the Wichita Public Library, contents not revealed <BR>|- 8/17: Jacob Allen; bound to rail road tracks <BR>|- 9/26: Carol Mould; c.o.d. unspecified, arson, items possibly missing from scene <BR>|- 11/30: WPD releases laundry list of clues &#40;view at catchbtk.com &#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/113004.pdf" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/113004.pdf</a>&#62;&#41; as to BTK&#39;s background and identity, asking for help from the public <BR>|- 12/8: unknown man, presumably BTK, calls quick mart alerting them to package left in Murdock Park; WPD searches park but finds nothing <BR>|- 12/14: citizen finds BTK package in Murdock Park containing Fox&#39;s drivers licence, as well as other unrevealed contents <BR>2002&#42;  <BR>6/4: Dorothy Slaughter beaten, died two weeks later, Mr. Slaughter &#40;survived&#41; beaten, telco cut, car keys stolen, home invasion <BR>2/20: body of Agnes Hayes found near bridge in Harvey County, KS; strangled, police believe crime originated in Wichita or Sedgwick County, known prostitute, body dumped [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_0128050047.shtml" target=_top>http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_ 0128050047.shtml</a>&#62; <BR>|- 10/17: Melvin D. Childress; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in field, car found 